# TripSense API requests
#
# open this file in VS Code with the REST Client extension and click Send Request
# above any block, or in IntelliJ click the green arrow
#
# the app must be running first
#   ./mvnw spring-boot:run
#
# add a new section here whenever you add an endpoint


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### chat - CS203-20
### needs ollama running, use + instead of spaces in the prompt
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### default prompt, no parameters
GET http://localhost:8080/chat

### simple question to check the model answers
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?prompt=name+three+cities+in+japan

### something closer to what we actually need it for
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?prompt=a+magnitude+6+earthquake+hit+hokkaido+today.+would+that+affect+a+ski+trip+to+niseko+next+week?+answer+yes+or+no+and+why

### one word answer, useful for checking how fast the model is
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?prompt=reply+with+only+the+word+ready

### long answer, this one is slow
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?prompt=explain+what+a+typhoon+is+in+three+paragraphs

### failure path
### stop ollama first, this should return a readable message and not a stack trace
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?prompt=hello


